  "id": "gahu_ewe",
  "name": "Gahu (Ewe recreational dance-drumming)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Recreational dance music that reached the Anlo-Ewe of Ghana from the Gun (Egun) people of the Benin–Nigeria coast in the mid-20th century, danced by clubs and cultural groups. The gankogui bell and axatse lay a four-beat timeline under the large boba (gboba) lead drum with sogo, kidi and kagan, and call-and-response songs. David Locke's 'Drum Gahu' documents it with recordings.",
  "recipe": "classic modern gahu, groove Percussion, west African branch. single leader group response. deep bass lead call-and-response boba, lead call-and-response sogo, kidi, kagan, interlocking timeline keeping gankogui, axatse. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
